      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:besa.thieving.monbba",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲁⲡⲣⲏ ⲣⲉⲃⲏ ⲛϩⲁϩ ⲛⲥⲟⲡ · ⲁⲩⲱ ⲁϥⲣⲕⲁⲕⲉ ϩⲛⲧⲡⲁϣⲉ ⲙⲡⲉϩⲟⲟⲩ · ⲁⲡⲕⲁⲕⲉ ϩⲟⲃⲥⲛ ⲙⲡⲛⲁⲩ ⲙ**ⲙⲉⲉⲣⲉ** · ⲛⲧⲉⲓϩⲉ ⲟⲛ ⲙⲡⲛⲣϩⲟⲧⲉ ⲙⲡⲉⲡⲉⲛϩⲏⲧ ⲁⲓⲥⲑⲁⲛⲉ · ⲟⲩⲇⲉ ⲙⲡⲉⲛϣⲧⲟⲣⲧⲣ · ⲁⲙⲡⲟⲗⲉⲙⲟⲥ ⲛⲙⲡⲣⲥⲱⲥ ⲙⲛⲛⲕⲉⲃⲁⲣⲃⲁⲣⲟⲥ ·",
      "english": "Similarly, if the sun were to hide itself times without number, and were to become dark at midday, and the darkness were to envelop us at noontide, still we should not be afraid, and our hearts would never feel troubled concerning it. And we should not be disturbed at the wars which break out with the Persians, and with the other barbarians,",
      "source": "The Asceticon of Apa Ephrem part 1",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:psephrem.asceticon.budge:1-23",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    }
